WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.782
The audit runs only on what the gate
kept, retain instances and consolidation

2
00:00:04.782 --> 00:00:08.775
targets, and its deliverable is
a per-instance compliance record.

3
00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:13.476
For each host it records every instance,
with version, edition and build,

4
00:00:13.476 --> 00:00:17.300
and the host operating system,
which sets the Arc envelope.

5
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:23.088
The Connected Machine agent runs on
Windows Server 2012 through 2025,

6
00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:29.076
SQL Server enabled by Arc needs 2016
or later, and the program sets its own

7
00:00:29.076 --> 00:00:35.163
floor at Windows Server 2019, because
2016 leaves support in January 2027.

8
00:00:35.163 --> 00:00:37.951
It records domain-join
state and whether the

9
00:00:37.951 --> 00:00:40.663
Arc agent and managed
identity are present.

10
00:00:40.663 --> 00:00:42.401
Then the authentication mode.

11
00:00:42.401 --> 00:00:45.047
The registry value LoginMode is one for

12
00:00:45.047 --> 00:00:48.175
Windows Authentication
mode and two for mixed.

13
00:00:48.175 --> 00:00:52.785
The audit cross-checks it against the
running instance with the Is Integrated

14
00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:57.324
Security Only server property, because
a mode change takes effect only after

15
00:00:57.324 --> 00:01:01.650
a restart, and any disagreement is an
anomaly to resolve before migrating.

16
00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:07.455
On SQL Server 2025 enabled by Arc it also
reads Is External Authentication Only,

17
00:01:07.455 --> 00:01:11.325
which shows the Disable
SQL Authentication setting.

18
00:01:11.325 --> 00:01:18.762
Every login is classified by its type in
sys.server_principals: U, a Windows user;

19
00:01:18.762 --> 00:01:22.080
G, a Windows group; S,
a SQL login; C and K,

20
00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:28.488
certificate- and key-mapped; and E
and X, Entra logins already present.

21
00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:31.675
The letters are the view's
values, not mnemonics.

22
00:01:31.675 --> 00:01:34.687
There's no type W, and
a query written against

23
00:01:34.687 --> 00:01:38.200
one returns zero rows and
reports a clean instance.

24
00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.447
Active SQL logins are a critical
finding, and an enabled SA with

25
00:01:42.447 --> 00:01:46.612
a non-rotated password is the
highest-priority finding of all.

26
00:01:46.612 --> 00:01:50.550
The audit captures the engine's
service account and checks its SPN.

27
00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:55.617
And each run is compared with the last:
a new SQL login, a revert to mixed mode,

28
00:01:55.617 --> 00:02:01.150
or a new passthrough linked server is
drift, and drift is a compliance violation.
